# Every text file checks out with LF on every platform.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: Git for Windows defaults core.autocrlf=true, so a Windows checkout rewrote
# HOSTS.md (and every other text file) to CRLF — and the generator gate, which asserts the
# checked-in file is byte-identical to what scripts/generate-hosts.mjs produces, failed on
# windows-latest against a file that was correct in the repository. The transcoding happened in
# the checkout, not in the content. holt is a git tool whose own tests reason about bytes; its
# repository does not invite the host's line-ending policy to edit it.
#
# Binary-ish assets are excluded from the text rule by their own patterns below.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.tgz binary
*.zip binary
